    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span><span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip bad\">Hard</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Two pointers</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Prefix max</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/trapping-rain-water/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 42</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Trapping Rain Water</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Water over a column = min(tallest bar on its left, tallest bar on its right) - its height. Two pointers find that min without the arrays: always settle the lower side, because the taller side already guarantees a wall. O(n) time, O(1) space.</p>\n"
